WEBVTT

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.240
Everyone's drinking.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:21.290
I'm hopeless, aren't I?

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.550
Getting all excited on my own...

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:27.250
And it turned out to be 
just a simple passageway.

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:30.490
Sawaki-kun, I apologize

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:33.050
for dragging you along and 
putting you through all that.

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:35.560
That's what was bothering you?

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:39.050
Hey, anyone would get curious if 
they saw an opening like that.

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:48.060
Oikawa... maybe I'm the 
one who should apologize.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:54.010
There's something I've 
been hiding from you.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:56.320
The professor and all the 
others know about it, too.

00:00:57.270 --> 00:01:00.830
You're the only one I haven't told.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:03.300
I'll tell you now.

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:05.080
Come with me, Oikawa.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.600
So, what did you want to tell me?

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:23.270
I...

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.350
can see microbes.

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:39.430
Hey, that ain't right!

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:42.700
The yellow malt fungus, 
Aspergillus oryzae.

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:49.550
I've hated the fact that I can 
see microbes since I was little.

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:53.960
Plus, bacteria and dirt and 
stuff really bother you, right?

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:56.960
So I just never said anything.

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:57.770
He told her!

00:01:57.770 --> 00:01:58.380
He did!

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:02.320
This ability is what got me 
dragged into Itsuki's seminar

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:03.890
right after I started at this school.

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:17.650
And what do you call this ability?

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:19.250
Huh?

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:22.110
Sawaki Attack?

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:23.660
Sawaki Special Hand?

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:27.570
If I had to call it something...

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:29.040
Single Spore Isolation?

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:34.350
Oikawa Single Spore Isolation!

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:37.860
How was that?

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:41.470
You got one. It's oryzae.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:46.240
You realize, Sawaki-kun, 
that microbes are extremely small.

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:48.230
Nobody can see them.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:52.910
Besides, it's obvious that you could 
catch malt fungus in a malt cellar.

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:54.230
D'oh!

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:56.510
I'm happy you tried,

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:59.010
but you have some weird ideas 
of encouragement, Sawaki-kun.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:03.060
Thanks, though. It was so stupid, 
it made me feel better.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:04.990
Let's go back to the others.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.340
Tadayasu, you confessed 
and got shot down!

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:13.830
It was an honorable defeat.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:16.000
That's not what it was.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:21.540
Oh, well.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:29.480
Moyashimon

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:29.480
Returns

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:56.440
{|fad(1150,1)}Fermenting Cellar

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:58.240
There.

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:02.570
Gingko nuts cooked in an envelope 
are my idea of an autumn snack.

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.570
They're really easy to prepare, huh?

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:07.150
By the way, the trick 
is to crack the shells

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:09.700
lightly with pliers before 
putting them in the microwave.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:12.650
This is the stuff.

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:13.700
They're pretty good.

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:16.680
They'd be perfect if we had some liquor,

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:18.210
but that wouldn't be a 
good idea at this hour.

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:21.400
These guys are totally ignoring 
how busy they should be.

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.460
Hey, Tadayasu! Get to work!

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:24.700
That's right!

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:28.170
Our buddies are working hard 
to make miso and soy sauce!

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:29.390
It's fine.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:30.930
It's our break time right now.

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:32.330
Microbes?

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:33.290
Yeah.

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:36.800
Speaking of which, 
I told Oikawa yesterday,

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:37.940
about how I can see microbes.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.330
Seriously?

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:40.140
Yeah.

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:43.650
And did the conversation 
progress to dating?

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:44.760
No.

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:46.450
I thought not.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.880
That's good, though.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:52.010
What happened with you 
guys after that, anyway?

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:53.450
With Hasegawa-san...

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:55.650
Nothing, obviously...

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:57.670
You know how she is.

00:05:57.670 --> 00:06:00.730
For us, it's like there's a 
trench that can't be filled,

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:02.210
a wall that can't be climbed.

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:03.870
I see.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:05.210
Good point.

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:06.960
Oh, that's right.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:09.290
Why don't we take some of 
these to the research lab?

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:11.430
We can't eat all these by ourselves.

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:12.220
Sure.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:18.290
Oh, Hasegawa-san.

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:19.980
What's in the envelope?

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:21.970
Gingko nuts.

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:24.710
Misato-san said to give them 
to you and the professor.

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:25.640
Oh...

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:26.550
Want some?

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:28.650
I'll pass.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:29.990
I'm in a hurry.

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:33.190
I checked online...

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:35.790
and the method most commonly 
used to patch a relationship

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:37.190
is going out for drinks together.

00:06:37.190 --> 00:06:39.000
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:42.410
Well... it sort of feels 
like there's a wall

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:45.500
between you, and Misato and Kawahama.

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:49.510
You do know what I'm like 
when I'm drunk, don't you?

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:52.260
Well, yeah, but...

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:56.040
Take those to the professor 
while they're still warm.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:56.910
Okay...

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.250
Professor Itsuki?

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:06.780
Hello, Hasegawa here.

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:08.760
Oh, Hasegawa-kun?

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:10.670
I wanted to ask a favor.

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:13.280
I'm going to have some wine. 
Could you go pick up some cheese?

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.050
Now?

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:17.200
Yes. Thanks a lot!

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:25.040
This is an announcement from 
the agricultural society.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:28.410
We had an exceptionally good 
soybean harvest this year,

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:30.230
so we request that all those

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:32.610
who can sell soybean products 
at their food stalls

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:34.550
at the harvest festival, please do so.

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:37.270
The harvest festival is 
right around the corner.

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:38.810
Little late to ask that now.

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:57.730
Was it really necessary to come for me?

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:01.100
I'm not going to run away or anything.

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:02.830
Just get in.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:10.060
Mutou's drunk again.

00:08:10.060 --> 00:08:10.840
Yeah.

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:13.980
Don't talk to me!

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:18.860
A big black car?

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:20.470
Is it Haruka-san?

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:26.480
You're one of Professor Itsuki's 
students, aren't you?

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:28.130
Huh?

00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:29.730
Well, yeah, pretty much.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:33.800
Why is a student coming to 
school drunk at this hour?

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:35.550
Never mind.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:40.220
Would you give this to 
Professor Itsuki for me?

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:41.450
Okay...

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:44.060
Got it.

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:52.140
It <i>was</i> Haruka-san!

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:57.220
Wow, you ate a lot.

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:58.960
We just couldn't stop.

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:01.000
Damn, I can't stand it anymore.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:03.000
I'm going to buy some drinks.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:06.250
Good idea, and the Hiyoshi Liquor 
Store was just remodeled, too.

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:11.040
Sawaki... you come with us...

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:15.120
And we'll get a discount from Yuuki.

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:15.890
Right.

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:19.740
Hiyoshi Liquor Store

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:19.740
Yuuki 
Liquor

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:19.740
You came at the perfect time!

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:24.150
Onii-chan just sent some good sake.

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:27.250
I was just about to call and 
invite you to drink some.

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:28.500
Really?

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.530
Way to go, Tomoharu!

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:31.580
Leave it to the aspiring TV star!

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:35.280
I don't think aspiring to be a TV 
star has anything to do with it.

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:37.520
Hey, kiddo, you're here.

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:39.260
That never ceases to amaze me.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:45.090
By the way, this is how 
Kikuji-san looks to Tadayasu.

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:57.440
Go on, drink up.

00:09:57.440 --> 00:09:59.910
This is a flavor you boys 
aren't familiar with.

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:01.420
We sure will.

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:02.810
Bottoms up!

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:05.040
I'll sample a bit, too.

00:10:12.070 --> 00:10:13.500
A woody fragrance...

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:15.730
Barreled sake? But it 
doesn't taste strong.

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:19.550
Yeah... Now that you 
mention it, it's not.

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:22.220
It's been diluted with water...

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:24.560
But there's more. 
It's two kinds of sake.

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:27.080
I'm impressed you figured all that out.

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:29.810
This sake is a special blend of mine.

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:32.090
A blend?

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:37.440
You mixed the sake that Onii-chan 
sent with some of your own?

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:38.570
Yes.

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:40.310
Can you do that?

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:43.700
It does go down easy, though.

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:45.860
Liquor dealers in the old days

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:48.440
sold sake out of the barrel by weight,

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:52.210
Something 
like 
H2O

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:53.210
Hehehehe...

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:51.920
so the sake they sold 
was what defined them.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:56.710
Tasty Sake!

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:53.670
If they only wanted money,

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:56.710
Something 
like 
H2O

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:55.510
they could just dump in a lot of water

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:56.710
to increase their stock.

00:10:56.710 --> 00:10:57.710
What?

00:10:57.710 --> 00:10:59.220
Greedy bastards.

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:04.130
But there's one thing that made them 
different from liquor dealers today.

00:11:04.130 --> 00:11:08.730
Back then, it wasn't just about 
keeping up their sake supplies.

00:11:09.220 --> 00:11:11.550
When you sell out of the 
barrel, and it gets warm,

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:14.820
it soaks up the fragrance of the 
barrel and changes the flavor.

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:17.820
By adding newly restocked sake to that,

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:19.530
they came up with their own

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:22.740
I've gotta let people drink 
this delicious sake!

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:22.740
exquisite flavors and 
created new batches.

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:25.320
They wanted to give their customers

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:27.120
the most delicious sake they could.

00:11:28.350 --> 00:11:32.000
You might say the pride and 
technique of sake dealers

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:36.130
earned customers' trust and brewed 
up camaraderie in the town.

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:40.130
Brew up camaraderie in a 
town... between people?

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:41.630
Yes.

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:45.360
In the old town, and even 
now, the liquor stores

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:47.310
Hiyoshi Liquor Store

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:47.320
are often the face of the town.

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:52.650
Yuuki 
Liquor

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:49.940
That's how rooted liquor stores 
were to their locations,

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:52.190
and how closely they 
existed with the area.

00:11:53.330 --> 00:11:56.900
That's something convenience stores 
and discount shops can't do.

00:11:57.220 --> 00:12:00.880
Of course, modern liquor stores 
don't have that power, either.

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:04.700
If the decline of liquor 
stores coincides

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:07.670
with the decline of the Japanese spirit,

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:12.540
then I'm glad to have been born in those days.

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:19.410
You all take your time.

00:12:21.730 --> 00:12:23.560
Isn't he amazing?

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:33.810
Notification of Withdrawal

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:41.570
Professor, I heard the agricultural 
society's announcement earlier.

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:43.930
What is the Itsuki seminar going to do?

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:47.410
Did something happen?

00:12:47.930 --> 00:12:49.910
Maybe...

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:53.830
I just know she got into a big 
whale of a car and took off!

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:57.600
I asked her to pick up some cheese 
so I could drink my wine.

00:12:57.600 --> 00:12:58.940
Now what will I do?

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:01.840
Hasegawa-san is quitting?

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:07.720
Allow me to take this matter 
into my own hands for now.

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:11.010
Hasegawa-kun will be all right.

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:18.930
Good work today.

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:21.440
Welcome back.

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:25.140
What's up? Did something happen?

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:27.600
Sort of.

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:32.300
Oh, yeah! We need to decide what the

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:34.880
Itsuki seminar is doing 
for the harvest festival.

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:36.150
You heard, right?

00:13:36.150 --> 00:13:39.460
All seminars have to run a 
food stall of some sort.

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:41.930
Misato-kun and Kawahama-kun

00:13:41.930 --> 00:13:44.040
aren't official members 
of the seminar yet,

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:46.530
but they do help in the 
fermenting cellar.

00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:51.460
Of course, I was hoping you and 
Sawaki-kun would help out, too.

00:13:51.460 --> 00:13:54.730
Misato-kun, Kawahama-kun, 
what do you two want to do?

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:56.170
What are you asking us for?

00:13:56.170 --> 00:13:58.930
You should be asking 
Hasegawa about that.

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:02.730
I can't handle getting whipped again 
for opening a stall by ourselves.

00:14:03.220 --> 00:14:07.200
But I thought we could decide 
on our own this year.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:08.340
But why?

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:10.240
Just a thought.

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:14.520
Well, we do have a little 
something underway already.

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:16.230
Yep. Squeak, squeak!

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:18.750
What does "Squeak, squeak" mean?

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:21.000
You'll find out eventually.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:25.450
Anyway, let's open a stall together 
as the fermenting cellar crew,

00:14:25.450 --> 00:14:27.630
and draw in the most customers.

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:30.650
There's prize money to be won, you know.

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:33.300
Prize money is definitely tempting.

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:36.660
It's fair to say that's the whole 
point of the harvest festival.

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:38.690
So let's come up with something,

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:39.900
even if Haruka-san isn't here.

00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:44.870
Then you can leave the 
stall to us. Right?

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:45.750
Indeed.

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:46.650
Squeak, squeak!

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:49.150
Once again, what does that mean?

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:50.510
Squeak, squeak!

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:52.160
That doesn't tell me anything!

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:59.130
All right, let's have a toast!

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:04.920
Your pasta will get cold.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:09.470
Aya-san, actually—

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:10.130
Holy crap!

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:12.490
No way! That's insane!

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:13.250
I know!

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:14.600
I don't believe it!

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:18.820
They're having a good time.

00:15:18.820 --> 00:15:21.440
Sorry. It's kinda noisy in here today.

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:26.380
Aww, you got too much head on that one.

00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:28.940
Stick to the seven to three ratio, okay?

00:15:29.640 --> 00:15:31.160
I'm sorry.

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:33.210
If we're too slack on the keg upkeep

00:15:33.210 --> 00:15:34.950
during this season, it foams up more.

00:15:35.420 --> 00:15:37.340
Shall I raise the air 
pressure for today?

00:15:37.340 --> 00:15:38.290
Yeah.

00:15:38.890 --> 00:15:41.890
Autumn is a nice season, 
but you know how it gets.

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:43.210
Liar...

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:45.310
Oh, a cocktail, huh?

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:45.960
Yes, sir.

00:15:46.350 --> 00:15:47.680
Did you know?

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:50.430
There's a certain way 
to handle the shaker.

00:15:50.430 --> 00:15:53.070
You raise your elbows to 
shoulder height like this,

00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:57.220
then hold your fingers like 
this... and the angle...

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:01.130
Wow, he's doing it with one hand!

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:05.730
Bet he's thinking, "How do you 
think you're making me look?!"

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:07.520
This is delicious!

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:12.290
Honestly, it's not good 
for him to be like that.

00:16:12.290 --> 00:16:14.130
I'll have to lecture him later.

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:15.280
Really?

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:17.490
You should've just told him.

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:19.060
It's better to throw

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:21.440
away the coarse foam that comes straight

00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:24.490
from the tap, and add finer 
foam to the beer later.

00:16:24.490 --> 00:16:26.380
Didn't you tell me that before?

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:29.550
Yeah, that is true.

00:16:30.140 --> 00:16:33.130
But it would have been 
pointless to say it then.

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:36.980
The old guy just wants 
to enjoy his drinks

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:39.640
and conversations with 
his drinking partner.

00:16:39.640 --> 00:16:41.720
Is that really it?

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:44.430
That's just what I think.

00:16:44.430 --> 00:16:47.150
Anyway, weren't you 
about to say something?

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:49.820
Oh... Well, actually...

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:52.680
Professor Itsuki said he'd 
do something about it,

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:56.910
so Sawaki-kun, Misato-senpai, 
and Kawahama-senpai don't know yet...

00:16:57.350 --> 00:16:59.010
But Hasegawa-san turned in

00:16:59.010 --> 00:17:01.410
a notice of withdrawal 
and left the school.

00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:02.680
What?

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:04.070
Whoa!

00:17:06.970 --> 00:17:08.170
You dumbass!

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:10.550
The hell are you doing? 
Don't get so drunk!

00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:13.210
Wow... he went too far.

00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:18.250
Those boys have already 
broken two glasses.

00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:20.310
Hey, you need to—

00:17:20.710 --> 00:17:22.500
Everyone all right?

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:24.560
Don't touch the glass.

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:25.810
I'll clean it up.

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:29.040
Sorry, man.

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:31.460
It's okay. No problem.

00:17:31.460 --> 00:17:34.990
Hey, dude, the chairs 
here are uncomfortable!

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:36.320
I just fell off mine!

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:38.450
Anyway, could I get a refill?

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:40.950
Yeah, you just spilled a whole glass!

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:42.920
Come on, have a drink with us!

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:45.960
I feel bad. Let me buy you a glass.

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:49.430
Sir, if you keep drinking like that,

00:17:49.430 --> 00:17:51.710
you'll ruin both our 
bar and your health.

00:17:55.450 --> 00:17:56.770
I'll wipe the table.

00:17:56.770 --> 00:17:58.730
Okay, thanks.

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:01.940
You guys got pretty drunk, huh?

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:04.350
Shall I get some water?

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:06.480
Okay... thanks.

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:08.510
G'night.

00:18:08.510 --> 00:18:10.480
Hey, you okay?

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:14.000
That really stopped the party.

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:16.990
He's so good at stuff like that.

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:20.490
He's not forceful, so you just feel

00:18:20.970 --> 00:18:22.490
at ease when he's around.

00:18:23.110 --> 00:18:25.820
Feeling at ease when 
they're around, huh...

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:25.130
Sorry for all the ruckus.

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:26.500
Good work.

00:18:27.070 --> 00:18:29.200
I wonder if the Itsuki seminar 
has anyone like that.

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:34.900
Maybe I'll try to be that way.

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:41.470
The 
Next 
Day

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:46.000
<i>The customer you are trying 
to reach is unable to answer.</i>

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:50.610
<i>Please leave a message after the tone.</i>

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:49.450
Still no answer today...

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:51.310
I guess that makes sense.

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:55.530
Notification of Withdrawal

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:54.760
I'm sure...

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:58.750
Where did you go, Haruka?

00:18:58.750 --> 00:19:02.800
Haruka! Come back!

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:16.920
You know, I really appreciate 
your father arranging this.

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:18.730
A pre-wedding trip...

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:20.830
I'm sure you're busy, too, Haruka-san.

00:19:20.830 --> 00:19:23.730
I'm really touched that 
you made time for me.

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:28.930
This is our chance to 
get much closer, eh?

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:32.690
I might just end up 
calling you "Haruka."

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:34.730
Just kidding.

00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:38.160
Oh, yeah, did you know?

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:42.450
Planes fly on the fares paid for first 
class and business class seats.

00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:47.500
Economy seats are just naturally 
sold by travel agencies, as well.

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:51.240
So it's no wonder there's so much 
difference between classes.

00:19:51.240 --> 00:19:53.690
Listen, could you let me sleep a little?

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:56.210
Wh-What?

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:58.160
<i>I don't know how he can</i>

00:19:58.160 --> 00:20:01.360
<i>blurt out such delusions with 
no hint of embarrassment.</i>

00:20:12.290 --> 00:20:13.610
<i>Oh, yeah...</i>

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:18.030
<i>The professor asked me to buy cheese...</i>

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.950
Moyashimon

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.950
Returns

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.950
Episode 4

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:52.950
Microbe 
Theater

00:21:50.400 --> 00:21:52.950
Microbe Theater Returns!

00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:52.950
Returns

00:21:55.630 --> 00:21:57.900
He's always such a sight.

00:21:58.450 --> 00:22:02.140
We yeasts are a lot that liquor dealers 
can't cut ties with, even if they try.

00:22:03.790 --> 00:22:04.880
You guys are...

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:05.630
6

00:22:05.630 --> 00:22:06.380
7

00:22:09.580 --> 00:22:12.670
We are the aces of sake 
production in the modern ages,

00:22:10.800 --> 00:22:13.890
Public Interest Organization  Brewing Society of Japan

00:22:12.670 --> 00:22:13.890
the kyokai yeasts!

00:22:14.670 --> 00:22:16.230
Kyokai yeasts?

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:16.230
Kyokai yeasts?

00:22:16.620 --> 00:22:19.650
Kyokai yeasts are yeasts 
distributed by the

00:22:19.650 --> 00:22:23.210
Brewing Society of Japan, 
a public interest organization,

00:22:23.210 --> 00:22:26.820
for making sake, shochu, and wine!

00:22:27.360 --> 00:22:30.240
You could call us the chosen elites!

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:31.160
Kyokai Yeast                                                                        Kyokai Yeast

00:22:31.040 --> 00:22:35.660
We kyokai yeasts are packed in 
ampoules like these to be sold.

00:22:35.860 --> 00:22:37.900
We wanna get started brewing now!

00:22:38.610 --> 00:22:40.950
It must be tough to be elite.

00:22:40.950 --> 00:22:44.430
By the way, our brand name is 
written in hiragana.

00:22:43.210 --> 00:22:46.970
Kyokai Yeasts

00:22:44.970 --> 00:22:46.480
Why is that?

00:22:47.970 --> 00:22:50.160
Because it's cuter!
